<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12969" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-lumbis</span></b> , e, adj.
		lumbus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>lamed in the loins, lamed</i> (post-Aug. and very
			rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">coturnix,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					10, 33, 51, § 103</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>weakened, enervated;
				weak, feeble</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">summā delumbe salivā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers.
					1, 104</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dietio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 16</span></i>
			.</div>
